  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B02",
   "act": "PACKET-IN-PRACTICE",
   "narration_text": "In practice, the packet is the first paragraph of the task prompt. 'Read the twelve meeting notes in slash weekly-notes and the tracker dot csv in slash project-data. Extract: completed items this week, items in the tracker not mentioned in any note, and action items with owners not in the tracker. Format as three-section markdown. Save to slash project-data slash outputs. Do not access any other folders. Do not send or share anything.' That is a scoped task.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "callout-reveal",
    "media": "media/B02.mp4",
    "manim": {
     "scene_class": "Scene_B02_ClaudeLiamCowork",
     "scenes_file": "scenes_std.py",
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B02.mp4",
      "at": "2026-07-25T10:37:20.220165"
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Packet example — explicit paths, three-section output, forbidden actions stated",
   "spark_line": "Name it. Bound it. Save it.",
   "estimated_duration_s": 14,
   "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
   "actual_duration_s": 23.49,
   "build": {
    "status": "SLATE",
    "src": null,
    "filled_by": null,
    "at": "2026-07-16T05:29:03",
    "needs": "PIPELINE → fill_slates/remotion_scenes for B02"
   }
  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B03",
   "act": "VERIFICATION-GATE",
   "narration_text": "The verification step comes after the run, but the criteria belong in the packet. You open the saved report. Does it have all three sections? Spot-check five tracker items against the notes. Check the action items list — are the owners correct? Are sensitive details exposed that should not appear? The verification criteria you write before the run are the checkable conditions you use after it. Without them, verification is just reading and hoping.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "callout-reveal",
    "media": "media/B03.mp4",
    "manim": {
     "scene_class": "Scene_B03_ClaudeLiamCowork",
     "scenes_file": "scenes_std.py",
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B03.mp4",
      "at": "2026-07-25T10:37:24.442924"
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Verification gate — section count / spot-check / owner check / exposure check",
   "spark_line": "Criteria in. Check after.",
   "estimated_duration_s": 12,
   "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
   "actual_duration_s": 22.12,
   "build": {
    "status": "SLATE",
    "src": null,
    "filled_by": null,
    "at": "2026-07-16T05:29:03",
    "needs": "PIPELINE → fill_slates/remotion_scenes for B03"
   }
  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B04",
   "act": "VERDICT",
   "narration_text": "A Cowork task without a written packet is guessing in both directions — Cowork guesses what it should read, and you guess whether the output is right. The packet collapses both guesses into a specification. What Cowork reads is named. What it may not read is named. What the output must contain is named. What verification looks like is named. The packet costs three minutes. The absent packet costs an afternoon of wrong output and a re-run.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "stagger",
    "remotion": {
     "pattern": "CoworkTaskView",
     "props": {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "type": "prompt",
        "text": "A Cowork task without a written packet is guessing in both directions"
       },
       {
        "type": "review",
        "items": [
         {
          "title": "Cowork guesses what to read",
          "badge": "Problem",
          "badgeTone": "fail"
         },
         {
          "title": "You guess whether output is correct",
          "badge": "Problem",
          "badgeTone": "fail"
         },
         {
          "title": "Written packet eliminates both guesses",
          "badge": "Fix",
          "badgeTone": "pass"
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "cues": [
       0,
       18,
       35
      ]
     },
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B04.mp4",
      "at": ""
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Artifact view — packet = named inputs / bounded access / stated criteria / checkable output",
   "spark_line": "Packet costs three minutes.",
